// 38_diag_envelopes.mty — v0.33 T4: structured agent-actionable diagnostics.
//
// @compile-error — this example is INTENDED to fail with MT4099. The
// codegen-sweep conformance tests skip files carrying this marker.
//
// What this file demonstrates
// ---------------------------
//
// Every `MTxxxx` Mighty emits now ships with a structured JSON
// envelope an agent can read and act on. The envelope carries
//
//   - the stable `MTxxxx` code,
//   - a 1-indexed span (file / line / col / byte_start / byte_end),
//   - the human title + multi-sentence prose,
//   - an optional `fix` block with one or more alternatives (each
//     with a unified-diff patch + rationale + confidence score),
//   - related codes and doc paths under `see_also`.
//
// The schema is documented at docs/internals/diagnostic-envelopes.md.
//
// Try it
// ------
//
//   # The classic pretty (ariadne) renderer — unchanged from v0.32:
//   mty check examples/38_diag_envelopes.mty
//
//   # The new structured envelope — one NDJSON line per diagnostic:
//   mty check examples/38_diag_envelopes.mty --format json
//
//   # Include a 3-line source snippet around each diagnostic:
//   mty check examples/38_diag_envelopes.mty --format json --include-source
//
// Marquee fix
// -----------
//
// The MT4099 envelope below ships THREE untaint alternatives — the
// regex-match strategy (highest confidence), the typed sanitizer
// strategy, and the enum allowlist strategy — letting the agent pick
// whichever fits the surrounding context. All three confidence values
// sit above the v0.33 0.5 emit-floor.
//
// Reference: docs/internals/taint-types.md, mty explain MT4099.
package diag_envelopes

use std.fs
use std.swarm

fn main() {
  let m = Member.anthropic("claude-opus-4-7")

  // ----- The tainted source ----------------------------------------
  //
  // `Member.ask(...)` is a documented tainted source. The compiler
  // tracks the binding through the rest of the function.
  let user_input = m.ask("What is the weather today?")

  // ----- The MT4099 compile-error site -----------------------------
  //
  // `std.fs.write` requires an untainted Str. Passing `user_input`
  // (which the type system tracks as Tainted[Str]) triggers MT4099.
  // The structured envelope an agent receives looks like:
  //
  //   {
  //     "code": "MT4099",
  //     "severity": "error",
  //     "span": {"file": "...", "line": 64, "col": 23, "len": 10, ...},
  //     "title": "tainted value flows to `std.fs.write` (arg #1) ...",
  //     "prose": "MT4099: Tainted value flows to a sensitive sink. ...",
  //     "fix": {
  //       "kind": "untaint",
  //       "confidence": 0.92,
  //       "alternatives": [
  //         {"label": "Constrain via a known-safe regex", ...},
  //         {"label": "Apply a provably-correct sanitizer", ...},
  //         {"label": "Parse against an enum allowlist", ...}
  //       ]
  //     },
  //     "see_also": ["MT4001", "docs/internals/taint-types.md"]
  //   }
  std.fs.write("log.txt", user_input)
}
